{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released","id":1524705,"title":"New W5 Glyphs Released","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-29T13:07:25-07:00","id":1524705,"title":"New W5 Glyphs Released","content":"As if some people didn't need another reason to dislike W5...<br /> <br /> As part of the &quot;Month of Darkness&quot; promotion, Paradox has released pack of various WOD5 illustrations for free use, across all three game lines. This includes logos, symbols, and dice designs. The W5 portion includes a selection of new glyphs, many of which weren't included in the rule book. These include glyphs for the five forms, tribal patrons, other major spirits, the four seasons (?!), and a few other important ones. Strangely enough, glyphs for the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers weren't included, although the BSD glyph was.<br /> <br /> Many of these glyphs are just outlines of what they kind of represent. For example, the glyphs for the five forms, in traditional order, are an open palm, a clenched fist, a wolf-man head and shoulders (including pointy ears), a large howling wolf head, and a normal wolf head. Some of the tribal patrons are no better. Now, the previous editions' glyphs looked liked what they represented as well. The new ones just do so with dashed-line outlines instead of less figurative means. Stag is just a diamond with stick antlers. North Wind is basically just a bunch of wavy lines. I can't even tell what Rat is. It looks more like a ram that anything else. <br /> <br /> Considering how complex the rest of the glyphs in the main book are, it is highly unlikely that the Garou would resort to something so simple for so many other 'words.' Many of the others are a little better, although I can't figure out why some were chosen to be included in this first batch of glyphs, such as Ally/Safety. I would have included the actual pics, but I'm not sure if they would be allowed. Also, I am not that tech savvy enough to be certain I know how to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:49:32-07:00","id":1524712,"title":"","content":"Ah, I can kinda see why some of those weren't in the corebook. The ones for the Forms and some of the ones for the Patron Spirits are symbols/logos rather than glyphs. Strange they included them in the package - while not including the ones for the non-player-Tribes. Also, the package has the logo for Endron and not Pentex which is weird because Endron is never mentioned in W5. Justin Achilli had explicitly mentioned before the release that the previous Pentex-subsidiaries wouldn't be part of W5.<br /> <br /> On a side-note: All the while, H5 still has no logos for the Creeds or pretty much anything else (aside from the H5-specific dice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:59:08-07:00","id":1524714,"title":"","content":"So to offer comparisons.<br /> <br /> Griffin (old)<br /> <br /> <img width=\"144\" height=\"163\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/0c/GlyphTotemGriffon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064354\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/0c/GlyphTotemGriffon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064354\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/0c/GlyphTotemGriffon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064354\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Griffin (new)<br /> <br /> <img width=\"137\" height=\"138\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/rXTeTqC.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rXTeTqC.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rXTeTqC.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Falcon (old)<br /> <img width=\"155\" height=\"208\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/c/cb/GlyphTotemFalcon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064303\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/c/cb/GlyphTotemFalcon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064303\" data-thumb-url=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/c/cb/GlyphTotemFalcon.png/revision/latest?cb=20180718064303\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Falcon (new)<br /> <img width=\"185\" height=\"127\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/X90WP0x.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/X90WP0x.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/X90WP0x.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Notice something? The old glyphs all had more information than just &quot;looks like the totem&quot;, they had an unified style which told you &quot;this is the glyph of a totem, not just a regular bird.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alone the new glyphs might seem fine, but,well. <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/thecyberrecord/glyphery/official-glyphs#h.ggjtnjiha233\" target=\"_blank\">They aren't MEANT to be alone.</a><br /> <br /> Glyphs are meant to be combined to create a story or a sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T14:12:26-07:00","id":1524715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1248\" height=\"536\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/KCa1Bs4.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KCa1Bs4.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KCa1Bs4.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> Or look at this: Crinos (left) and Lupus (right). Those are <i>not </i>glyphs. Those are stylized symbols of Forms as a game-element with an emphasis on being readable to the players at the table. These aren't representations of an in-game Garou-language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T14:57:56-07:00","id":1524716,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they knew what the old glyphs meant and how they were constructed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T16:44:57-07:00","id":1524717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524716#post1524716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they knew what the old glyphs meant and how they were constructed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they believe that part was irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T20:36:31-07:00","id":1524732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524716#post1524716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they knew what the old glyphs meant and how they were constructed?</div> </div> </div> </div>They clearly didn't care. After all, there was no reason to not just do a copy-paste with the old Tribe-glyphs and yet they were all &quot;re-designed&quot;. But in this case &quot;re-designed&quot; always meant to add new lines to the glyphs that didn't take the old lore into consideration. And the new &quot;glyphs&quot; from the package just add to that bad vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T00:49:14-07:00","id":1524740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524717#post1524717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess they believe that part was irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling it was that and to avoid making the game TOO complicated for new players. But, personally, removing ALL the complicated things leaves a game with little depth. Glyphs especially were something that you wouldn't have to worry about unless you were into that stuff and then they offered a LOT of extra stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T03:03:24-07:00","id":1524741,"title":"","content":"I think the main-reason for W5's visual changes is that V5 had different symbols for the Clans and so similarly it was reasoned that W5 should have different symbols for things. But if you look back at the V5 corebook, there's that whole sidebar on pg 54 called &quot;Iconography&quot; discussing the changes and how the old symbols are also still valid. Fast forward to 2022 and you have a different WOD-team that is wholly uninterested in lore/worldbuilding. So now the symbols/&quot;glyphs&quot; are just... different. No reasoning as to why or how. It's just different, that's all. And it's no wonder that with that lack of vision you tell an artist to come up with &quot;glyphs&quot; for the five forms, they just give you these obvious symbols like the outline of a wolf's head for the Lupus-form or presenting a different version of any Tribe-glyph just ends up being about adding a few lines here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T04:15:38-07:00","id":1524744,"title":"","content":"Previous books like general Dark Ages, Veil of Night, and Victorian Age also already established that vampires symbols varied over time and place (in theory you could count KotEK as well). So updated symbols (esp. after major breaches in security, Clan shake-ups, and so on) make sense with the previous game lines. The WtA games in stark contrast held that Garou glyphs have largely stayed the same in basic meaning, with only more poetic/interpretation drifts and addition of new symbols for new phenomenon happening over time.<br /> <br /> Did anything in this art asset drop explain what the new Shadow Lord symbol is supposed to represent? The other significantly changed ones are at least things that you can intuit fairly easily (ex: the new Silver Fang one is supposed to be a crown because they're the leader/ruler Tribe and all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T04:54:58-07:00","id":1524748,"title":"","content":"No, the asset-drop didn't come with any explanations.<br /> <br /> I've looked through the W5-corebook to see how the book handles Garou-language and glyphs. The first thing is that it doesn't seem like it's ever acknowledged that the Garou have their own language. Instead, the &quot;language of spirits&quot; is mentioned and other than that it's about human languages a Garou may grow up with. For example, here on pg 45 in the Werewolf Names sidebar: &quot;Garou names may reflect the cultural norms and mother tongue of the Garou\u2019s homeland, or they may become quite esoteric, and even borrow from the language of spirits.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> The glyphs are both treated as symbols and an alphabet. Like here in the section The Litany on pg 46: &quot;Many \u2014 probably most \u2014 Garou know the Litany in some form, whether verbatim as presented here, via a series of parables, or perhaps even as a series of lupus- scratched warning glyphs on a pile of stacked stones at the edge of the Schwarzwald.\u200b&quot; (man, that lupus must have done a lot of scratching to get the entirety of the Litany on that pile of stacked stones...). Then there's a bit in the sample-adventure where a test is described whether the PCs are able to recognize that they are in a dead caern that used to belong to the Cult of Fenris (pg 306): &quot;On a Difficulty 3 Wits + Awareness test, the characters find a number of smooth soapstone rocks with runes carved into them buried. Also buried are a number of crystals carved into spear points. Characters who succeed at a Difficulty 2 Intelligence + Occult test recognize the runes as werewolf glyphs and the spear points as serving some kind of Rite purpose, but unconnected to the murder-ritual. A critical win recognizes them as Cult of Fenris runes as well.\u200b&quot; Well, as we all know Tribes in W5 have no connection to human culture or ethnicity whatsoever. That's why the Native American Tribes were completely rewritten. It's not like there's any sort of cultural link here when while discussing the Cult of Fenris the glyphs are called &quot;runes&quot;... sigh<br /> <br /> Then there's the Wyrm-Loresheet where the first dot is this (pg 299): &quot;Garou who knows the glyph can represent the Black Spiral, but among servitors of the Wyrm, the glyph itself<br /> possesses nuances that most Garou don\u2019t know. You know how to convincingly make the true Black Spiral glyph, which you might use as bait or to mislead others, but those who know you possess this ability are suspicious of you, if not outright hostile.&quot; Here you get some notion that there are nuances to a glyph and somehow most Garou don't know about those when it comes to the Black Spiral glyph. Together with the bit in the adventure about the Cult of Fenris &quot;runes&quot;, it seems like glyphs are yet another area in W5 where Garou are a bit clueless for the most part.<br /> <br /> Well, anyway, it's really more about &quot;Garou have glyphs and can read them on a successful Intelligence + Occult test.&quot;. But there's no mention of a specific Garou-language or any exploration of where those glyphs come from or how they are used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T05:27:46-07:00","id":1524750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524744#post1524744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Did anything in this art asset drop explain what the new Shadow Lord symbol is supposed to represent? The other significantly changed ones are at least things that you can intuit fairly easily (ex: the new Silver Fang one is supposed to be a crown because they're the leader/ruler Tribe and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a guess, but the symbol seems to symbolize something hidden from the moon or a bunch of shadows piled together, symbolizing the clan's discretion. At least that's how I interpret this bunch of scratches(?).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T05:36:16-07:00","id":1524752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524744#post1524744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anything in this art asset drop explain what the new Shadow Lord symbol is supposed to represent? The other significantly changed ones are at least things that you can intuit fairly easily (ex: the new Silver Fang one is supposed to be a crown because they're the leader/ruler Tribe and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was a dagger/klaive piercing the skin and burying deep in someone's back?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T10:43:48-07:00","id":1524760,"title":"","content":"So going through the glyphs, two concepts made me stop.<br /> <br /> There are glyphs for Gaia's Howl ANd The Bite. Not 'a bite', THE bite.<br /> <br /> So we might be seeing virus wolves soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T12:31:24-07:00","id":1524762,"title":"","content":"The thing about low-Wyrm lore Garou not being able to fully comprehend the nuances of Wyrm-glyphs even if they can more or less recognize the Black Spiral glyph and could theoretically reproduce it (even if this might be looked askance at by other Garou) is actually interesting imo and offers some compelling ideas for things which might be further developed upon, regardless of how one feels about the new W5 glyphs.<br /> <br /> The notion of fleshing out how the Garou can use their glyphs/language, both for practical purposes, but its social and political implications is very interesting imo. It might be something worthwhile to look for inspiration from irl beliefs about the spiritual/magical powers of writing systems. Perhaps the reason why it would be looked at with suspicion to know the Black Spiral rune is that merely being able to read it, much less reproduce it, really does provide an extra route by which a Garou might become the subject of Wyrm influence or molestation. One could further flesh this out as part of what Older Brother/Ghost Council and the Shadow Lords do which make other Garou somewhat uneasy; they learn the fallen tongues and do expose themselves to serious risks in exchange for the knowledge and power which that brings.<br /> <br /> Leaving the glyphs themselves aside, I do think there\u2019s room there for a development of that concept for in-setting uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T15:55:50-07:00","id":1524774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524762#post1524762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about low-Wyrm lore Garou not being able to fully comprehend the nuances of Wyrm-glyphs even if they can more or less recognize the Black Spiral glyph and could theoretically reproduce it (even if this might be looked askance at by other Garou) is actually interesting imo and offers some compelling ideas for things which might be further developed upon, regardless of how one feels about the new W5 glyphs.<br /> <br /> The notion of fleshing out how the Garou can use their glyphs/language, both for practical purposes, but its social and political implications is very interesting imo. It might be something worthwhile to look for inspiration from irl beliefs about the spiritual/magical powers of writing systems. Perhaps the reason why it would be looked at with suspicion to know the Black Spiral rune is that merely being able to read it, much less reproduce it, really does provide an extra route by which a Garou might become the subject of Wyrm influence or molestation. One could further flesh this out as part of what Older Brother/Ghost Council and the Shadow Lords do which make other Garou somewhat uneasy; they learn the fallen tongues and do expose themselves to serious risks in exchange for the knowledge and power which that brings.<br /> <br /> Leaving the glyphs themselves aside, I do think there\u2019s room there for a development of that concept for in-setting uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very similar situation came up when there were some Gaians interacting with a Wyrm-glyph in the W20 novel, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/150855/W20-The-Poison-Tree\" target=\"_blank\">The Poison Tree</a>, which also illustrates one of my favorite parts of glyphs \u2014 their spiritual resonance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Poison Tree, page 59</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cLook at this.\u201d<br /> <br /> She tapped a claw on the polished surface of the table. Symbols had been carved there, where Eleanor could see them. There were a several more strange glyphs, similar to the garou\u2019s written language but there was something about the odd curves and jagged lines that both intrigued Ingrid and repelled her. They surrounded a larger symbol: a crude set of nested circles, like a target. <i>Or perhaps an attempt at a spiral?</i><br /> <br /> \u201cThere is a message here,\u201d the Theurge mused. \u201cBut what it means is beyond me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you recognize the symbols?\u201d Ingrid asked.<br /> <br /> Anna sniffed. \u201cSpirit glyphs,\u201d she observed. \u201cSymbols representing potent mystical truths.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSuch as?\u201d<br /> <br /> The garou shaman\u2019s expression turned guarded, as all Theurges do when prodded with questions about the spirit realm. \u201cI don\u2019t know. And I\u2019m not sure I want to know.\u201d She shook her head. \u201cI don\u2019t like the way they\u2026call to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ingrid scowled at the glyphs. She reached down and, one by one, scratched through each symbol. She was surprised \u2013 and more than a little unsettled \u2013 at how hard it was to bring herself to do it, but the last thing she wanted was to let some fool of a mortal get a good look at them.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:52:19-07:00","id":1524780,"title":"","content":"A thing with W5 is very often with lore is that things have been removed without any care for what that does to the lore/worldbuilding of the game. Any good idea you might get from what W5 is doing is 90% the reader adding their own ideas. Like the idea of forbidden glyphs as mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2810_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2810\" data-vbnamecard=\"2810\">Yakecen-Sings</a> : It wouldn't actually quite work with the tone the Loresheet is striking in the W5 corebook. First, this is the reason where this argument arises that the W5 corebook allows you to redeem Black Spiral Dancers but not Cult of Fenris members. There's a strangely collegial tone in how Wyrm-followers are talked about on that Loresheet. For example, the two-dot-bit talks about your PC being friends with a &quot;remarkably stable Fomor&quot;, a Black Spiral Dancer or a vampire (I guess the writer there forgot there wasn't supposed to be any inherent connection between vampires and the Wyrm anymore). From there you learn about Wyrm-follower-specific hideouts you can use and other stuff. The Loresheet is about your character being close to Wyrm-followers with the five-dot being the ability to redeem a Black Spiral Dancer by convincing them to &quot;emancipate themselves&quot; (that's how the Loresheet phrases it). And the drawback is always that other Garou will like you less for using Wyrm-affiliated resources. But that's all. After all, Wyrm-taint isn't a thing in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T17:13:36-07:00","id":1524781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524780#post1524780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing with W5 is very often with lore is that things have been removed without any care for what that does to the lore/worldbuilding of the game. Any good idea you might get from what W5 is doing is 90% the reader adding their own ideas. Like the idea of forbidden glyphs as mentioned by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2810_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2810\" data-vbnamecard=\"2810\">Yakecen-Sings</a> : It wouldn't actually quite work with the tone the Loresheet is striking in the W5 corebook. First, this is the reason where this argument arises that the W5 corebook allows you to redeem Black Spiral Dancers but not Cult of Fenris members. There's a strangely collegial tone in how Wyrm-followers are talked about on that Loresheet. For example, the two-dot-bit talks about your PC being friends with a &quot;remarkably stable Fomor&quot;, a Black Spiral Dancer or a vampire (I guess the writer there forgot there wasn't supposed to be any inherent connection between vampires and the Wyrm anymore). From there you learn about Wyrm-follower-specific hideouts you can use and other stuff. The Loresheet is about your character being close to Wyrm-followers with the five-dot being the ability to redeem a Black Spiral Dancer by convincing them to &quot;emancipate themselves&quot; (that's how the Loresheet phrases it). And the drawback is always that other Garou will like you less for using Wyrm-affiliated resources. But that's all. After all, Wyrm-taint isn't a thing in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they took out the kegare-like bits of Triatic influence, but they didn't do anything to make any of the characters noted as being of the Wyrm nicer, so it doesn't really matter. Banes still get attracted to people doing terrible shit and feed off them or possess them, vampires still shit up their surroundings, and BSDs are still into every kind of terrible abuse every which way but consensual. So basically, it just removes any kind of check on flat out killing an SOB if you catch them red-handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T17:22:58-07:00","id":1524782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524781#post1524781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they took out the kegare-like bits of Triatic influence, but they didn't do anything to make any of the characters noted as being of the Wyrm nicer, so it doesn't really matter. Banes still get attracted to people doing terrible shit and feed off them or possess them, vampires still shit up their surroundings, and BSDs are still into every kind of terrible abuse every which way but consensual. So basically, it just removes any kind of check on flat out killing an SOB if you catch them red-handed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Loresheet on pg 299 I'm specifically talking about. That's where this gets weird. That Loresheet is all about your character being chummy with Wyrm-followers and knowing their secrets. And the detriment is that when other Garou find out about it they like you less. And ultimately you can convert a BSD to become a believer in Gaia again. But the tone of that Loresheet is the complete opposite of horror and instead frames knowing Wyrm-followers as a mere group of &quot;bad kids&quot; you hang out with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T17:35:40-07:00","id":1524783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524782#post1524782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the Loresheet on pg 299 I'm specifically talking about. That's where this gets weird. That Loresheet is all about your character being chummy with Wyrm-followers and knowing their secrets. And the detriment is that when other Garou find out about it they like you less. And ultimately you can convert a BSD to become a believer in Gaia again. But the tone of that Loresheet is the complete opposite of horror and instead frames knowing Wyrm-followers as a mere group of &quot;bad kids&quot; you hang out with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That smacks of someone who thought that BSDs were just like the Sabbat for W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T02:08:03-07:00","id":1524797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524783#post1524783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That smacks of someone who thought that BSDs were just like the Sabbat for W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and did not read the book proper. Because even W5 is clear that banes and their ilk are spirits of corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T03:32:49-07:00","id":1524801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524783#post1524783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That smacks of someone who thought that BSDs were just like the Sabbat for W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the whole approach on that Loresheet doesn't quite make sense. Like the third dot is about your character knowing about one of the hideouts Wyrm-followers in the local area use and having the ability to use the hideout themselves. But that's strange because if a Garou had that knowledge why wouldn't they use that to go after the Wyrm-followers...? Why would the reaction to finding a hideout for Wyrm-followers be &quot;Oh cool, new hangout-spot discovered!&quot;? And like usual the caveat is that if other Garou discover what your character knows &quot;your character has likely much to answer for&quot; as the text puts it. And the fourth dort is about a mighty Wyrm-spirit being unable to harm your character and showing deference to your character because of some pact in some long forgotten past. And it's called a &quot;great arrangement&quot; with the usual drawback that if other Garou find out about it, your character will get into trouble. But what's the idea here? That your character turns that Wyrm-spirit into an ally? But that would be absurd, of course. And of course the fifth dot is about your character once per story being able to try to get a Black Spiral Dancer to switch sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T08:12:51-07:00","id":1524806,"title":"","content":"The dumbest thing is that you could switch the BSD thing with CoF and it'd make more sense. Since CoF ARE still on the same side, using their stuff makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:19:16-07:00","id":1524811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524806#post1524806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dumbest thing is that you could switch the BSD thing with CoF and it'd make more sense. Since CoF ARE still on the same side, using their stuff makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And of course, it just gets even more ludicrous when we then had something like that adventure Deepest of Wounds where a Cult of Fenris member is using torture and brainwashing to convert new members. But then you have this Loresheet where with the second dot you can get a Black Spiral Dancer buddy and with the fifth dot you get the ability to redeem BSD-Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T13:12:49-07:00","id":1524827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524801#post1524801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, the whole approach on that Loresheet doesn't quite make sense. Like the third dot is about your character knowing about one of the hideouts Wyrm-followers in the local area use and having the ability to use the hideout themselves. But that's strange because if a Garou had that knowledge why wouldn't they use that to go after the Wyrm-followers...? Why would the reaction to finding a hideout for Wyrm-followers be &quot;Oh cool, new hangout-spot discovered!&quot;? And like usual the caveat is that if other Garou discover what your character knows &quot;your character has likely much to answer for&quot; as the text puts it. And the fourth dort is about a mighty Wyrm-spirit being unable to harm your character and showing deference to your character because of some pact in some long forgotten past. And it's called a &quot;great arrangement&quot; with the usual drawback that if other Garou find out about it, your character will get into trouble. But what's the idea here? That your character turns that Wyrm-spirit into an ally? But that would be absurd, of course. And of course the fifth dot is about your character once per story being able to try to get a Black Spiral Dancer to switch sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point in the championship, I don't even think it's that strange, I mean, if the Garou nation fell, or never existed, who knows, and the tribes just fight for survival and to satisfy their interests, it wouldn't be strange for them to not have the slightest respect or caution for Garou traditions that we know, the rules have fallen so to speak, neither the wyrm and the weaver seem to be proper enemies, except in cases like the Red Talons, but this raises two questions for me, the first is what would be the objective besides surviving? The second is simply: WHY do it this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T13:46:16-07:00","id":1524830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524827#post1524827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point in the championship, I don't even think it's that strange, I mean, if the Garou nation fell, or never existed, who knows, and the tribes just fight for survival and to satisfy their interests, it wouldn't be strange for them to not have the slightest respect or caution for Garou traditions that we know, the rules have fallen so to speak, neither the wyrm and the weaver seem to be proper enemies, except in cases like the Red Talons, but this raises two questions for me, the first is what would be the objective besides surviving? The second is simply: WHY do it this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a huge irony in going down that road, I think. Let's assume you can use the W5-setting to justify it: The Garou-Nation has fallen, the Litany is a joke (either it's Elders exploiting it or young Garou ignoring/disrespecting it), it's the age of Apocalypse and Gaia's dead/dying. And in all that turmoil the lines between friend and enemy aren't so clear anymore. And there's no more &quot;Kill the minions of the Wyrm on sight!&quot;-policy anymore for Garou - and that's what gets you that kind of Loresheet.<br /> <br /> If all of that is true, the huge irony is that the Cult of Fenris are the good guys then. They are absolutely right to look down on the other Garou after all. The Cult of Fenris are the only Garou still invested in being the warriors of Gaia. At least, they're trying to take the fight to their enemies. Even ignoring the torture/brainwashing-scene in the Deepest of Wounds adventure, the Cult of Fenris venturing out to fight the Wyrm with other volunteers from other Tribes is portrayed as misguided and pointless... but on the other hand, what exactly did the Garou who stayed behind accomplish in contrast? They sat in their caern, protected it while the world is getting worse and worse and... that's about it.<br /> <br /> Like you said, W5 is setting up a scenario where survival is the highest thing to aspire to. And I guess in light of that, maybe it isn't so hard to imagine that your Garou-characters are just gonna start hanging out with BSD-characters because... who cares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T13:54:15-07:00","id":1524831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524811#post1524811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And of course, it just gets even more ludicrous when we then had something like that adventure Deepest of Wounds where a Cult of Fenris member is using torture and brainwashing to convert new members. But then you have this Loresheet where with the second dot you can get a Black Spiral Dancer buddy and with the fifth dot you get the ability to redeem BSD-Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna need more than truth bullets for that, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T13:59:45-07:00","id":1524832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524831#post1524831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna need more than truth bullets for that, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funniest part of Deepest of Wounds to me is that there are Garou who want to join the Cult of Fenris (and in the final confrontation will side with the Fenrir against the PCs) and venture out there to fight the Wyrm but the Cult of Fenris for whatever reason still kidnap another Garou and try to torture/brainwash them to get them on their side... It's not like the Cult of Fenris even needs to do this! It's just really hamfisted signaling to say &quot;Don't forget! They are the bad guys!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:08:33-07:00","id":1524834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524832#post1524832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funniest part of Deepest of Wounds to me is that there are Garou who want to join the Cult of Fenris (and in the final confrontation will side with the Fenrir against the PCs) and venture out there to fight the Wyrm but the Cult of Fenris for whatever reason still kidnap another Garou and try to torture/brainwash them to get them on their side... It's not like the Cult of Fenris even needs to do this! It's just really hamfisted signaling to say &quot;Don't forget! They are the bad guys!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just keep thinking back to the creative director's insistence that the Get somehow have something to answer for in spite of being entirely fictional and only what they're written to be, even when not being written to have anything to do with the SoH. Like how at present, they're being written to be bad knockoffs of the Remnants of Despair from Danganronpa, and how this isn't somehow the essential nature of any part of the splat, just a terrible decision for the line's direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:08:44-07:00","id":1524835,"title":"","content":"The weird thing for me is that the author writes some exceptionally complex and moving material for Savage Age but the stuff they've written for W5 so far is mostly just clown shoes......part of me is thinking ( hoping) there's a bunch of top down interference like there was with W20 material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:12:35-07:00","id":1524836,"title":"","content":"It'd probably be easier to think of things that weren't a result of top-down interference. Someone's got an axe to grind, and they put him in charge of the entire show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:15:39-07:00","id":1524837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524835#post1524835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing for me is that the author writes some exceptionally complex and moving material for Savage Age but the stuff they've written for W5 so far is mostly just clown shoes......part of me is thinking ( hoping) there's a bunch of top down interference like there was with W20 material.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Savage Age is a personal project while Deepest Wounds was a commission work. Essentially, if the client wants Remnants of De-I mean Cult of Fenris torturing? That's what the client gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:24:29-07:00","id":1524839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524835#post1524835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing for me is that the author writes some exceptionally complex and moving material for Savage Age but the stuff they've written for W5 so far is mostly just clown shoes......part of me is thinking ( hoping) there's a bunch of top down interference like there was with W20 material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I got the feeling that adventure was originally written with the BSD in mind, but editorial mandate changed it to Cult of Fenris partway through. And they were either too far along or just didn't care enough to rework the adventure to make it fit. (Or this was the editorial intent, to make the Fenrir maximum evil, because they have an ax to grind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T17:01:03-07:00","id":1525001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1524835#post1524835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing for me is that the author writes some exceptionally complex and moving material for Savage Age but the stuff they've written for W5 so far is mostly just clown shoes......part of me is thinking ( hoping) there's a bunch of top down interference like there was with W20 material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently he was in their Discord defending this adventure path. Which like. Why. I love Savage Age so much, but you'd think someone who understands the lore well enough to write a 3PP that good would know why this is terrible. Maybe it's just not wanting to trash something he got paid for or an NDA or something, I hope. Because otherwise, damn.<br /> <br /> Though, at the same time Weaponized Ink is a team and he's only been the sole writer on one book in that project, so maybe he's really talented at developing games, but not good at writing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T00:18:02-07:00","id":1525014,"title":"","content":"For the sake of argument, let's assume the adventure WAS originally designed with BSDs as the antagonists. Would that make the adventure path better? Genuine question.<br /> <br /> Like, are we just getting tripped up by how wildly out of character the Fenrir are acting? Is THAT the problem? Or are there deeper issues at play that mar the adventure's quality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T05:20:29-07:00","id":1525019,"title":"","content":"I think even if you ignore the previous editions and just want to go with the version of the Cult of Fenris as presented in the W5 corebook, there are issues in how they are portrayed.<br /> <br /> In the adventure within the corebook called No Matter How Small you get two weird bits about the Fenrir. One, the Fenrir have abandoned a caern to look for Wyrm-followers to fight but it's established that when the PCs re-awaken the caern and settle down in it, now all of a sudden the Fenrir want the caern back. They care so little that they were willing to just abandon it but they also care so much about the caern that the moment other Garou move in they will intervene...? It's weird. Two, you never meet any Fenrir-Garou but instead you get to interact with Cult of Fenris' human allies - which is also weird. Why would this supposedly extremist Garou-tribe bother with human allies? Kinfolk isn't a thing anymore after all. There's also that lingering connotation again with the two human allies being portrayed as stereotypical rednecks. And I think what would make more sense here as well is that when the main-antagonist of this adventure who is a lone Fomor does his ritual at the abandoned caern one of the side-effects is that it attracts the attention of BSD rather than the Cult of Fenris. The Cult is out there looking for a good fight. And it would make more sense for the Fenrir only to start caring about the caern again once BSD start to move in. And so the follow-up to the adventure is a three-way-fight between the BSD, Fenrir and the PC-Pack rather than the straight-up PCs vs Fenrir contest the adventure advices the ST to pursue after the adventure.<br /> <br /> With the Renegade-adventure Deepest of Wounds it's set up that until five years ago your local Sept was neighbors with a Cult of Fenris caern without any issues but then <i>somehow </i>their caern &quot;dried up&quot;. And that's when the Cult of Fenris left and gave out the call that they wanted other Garou to join them (which some did). Then this adventure starts when the survivors of this mini-crusade come back to look for more resources and new recruits. What's weird is that without the whole kidnapping/torture/brainwashing-sub-plot all this would be about is the disagreement between Garou who think staying and guarding the caern is more important than venturing out to look for enemies and those who think something needs to be done about the miserable state of the world. And the easiest way to make sense of the kidnapping/torture/brainwashing-stuff is if these Garou who come back are actually converted BSD. On their mini-crusade these survivors got corrupted and fell to the Wyrm. So yeah, I think bringing BSD into this would make this adventure better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T05:57:02-07:00","id":1525021,"title":"","content":"On top of everything, it bears repeating; Cult of Fenris are not on the side of the Wyrm, they are not on the side of the Weaver. They are as much Gaian as the PCs and just have more extreme methods and a poorly thought-out insanity.<br /> <br /> There are plots that could create conflict, but neither No Matter How Small nor Deepest Wounds use them. Instead, they either randomly add kinfolk back in OR the CoF use BSD methods that make no sense for their culture nor how Hauglosk works. Because they want to be 100% certain we know the CoF are evil.<br /> <br /> Which is sad, because you can do so much with the conflict between moderation and extreme action. But that requires both sides to have a point, which the CoF are not afforded.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T06:08:39-07:00","id":1525022,"title":"","content":"Additionally, another reason to imagine that the kidnapping/torture/brainwashing-subplot originally was about BSD is that the device/method used for the brainwashing is called the &quot;Maggot Symphony&quot;. That's a <i>very </i>Wyrm-y name. The cultural connection that's usually present (despite W5 supposedly being about removing that sort of thing) with the Cult of Fenris is all that Nordic/Viking-imagery stuff. Using something called &quot;Maggot Symphony&quot; seems rather out-of-place for that Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T09:54:48-07:00","id":1525024,"title":"","content":"Also the rest of the Sept just sitting around sucking their thumbs while the Caern is drained and destroyed is............WTF?<br /> <br /> I mean, unless they are all in deep, deep Harano and even then the destruction of a Caern is the kind of thing that would break most Garou out of Harano at least temporarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T15:19:27-07:00","id":1525035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525024#post1525024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the rest of the Sept just sitting around sucking their thumbs while the Caern is drained and destroyed is............WTF?<br /> <br /> I mean, unless they are all in deep, deep Harano and even then the destruction of a Caern is the kind of thing that would break most Garou out of Harano at least temporarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's part of the setup. It just says: &quot;Five or so years ago, a nearby caern, a Garou spiritual nexus, died. The dead caern was controlled by the Cult of Fenris. Despite feverish work by the caern\u2019s Fenrir defenders, as well as aid from the players\u2019 caern, the caern\u2019s spirit energies dried up.\u200b&quot; That's why I emphasized the &quot;somehow&quot;. This description just assumes that it has happened... <i>somehow</i>.<br /> <br /> It's also striking how the Cult of Fenris (together with Garou from other Tribes) venturing out to fight the Wyrm is portrayed as wrongheaded but meanwhile, there's no description of the ones just hunkering down in the remaining caerns achieving anything either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T16:33:58-07:00","id":1525044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525035#post1525035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's part of the setup. It just says: &quot;Five or so years ago, a nearby caern, a Garou spiritual nexus, died. The dead caern was controlled by the Cult of Fenris. Despite feverish work by the caern\u2019s Fenrir defenders, as well as aid from the players\u2019 caern, the caern\u2019s spirit energies dried up.\u200b&quot; That's why I emphasized the &quot;somehow&quot;. This description just assumes that it has happened... <i>somehow</i>.<br /> <br /> It's also striking how the Cult of Fenris (together with Garou from other Tribes) venturing out to fight the Wyrm is portrayed as wrongheaded but meanwhile, there's no description of the ones just hunkering down in the remaining caerns achieving anything either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to Black Lung in Deepest of Wounds. The entire Sept sits and watches him destroy a Caern..........which is kinda weird if the Nations and Cults biggest failing is supposed to be that they act/ed too quickly and violently.<br /> <br /> Cos doing jack shit doesn't seem to accomplish much either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T17:25:57-07:00","id":1525046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525044#post1525044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm referring to Black Lung in Deepest of Wounds. The entire Sept sits and watches him destroy a Caern..........which is kinda weird if the Nations and Cults biggest failing is supposed to be that they act/ed too quickly and violently.<br /> <br /> Cos doing jack shit doesn't seem to accomplish much either.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read that I was so utterly confused. You have a hostile external element doing an abhorrent thing and you have reservations because... what? People don't know his allegiance? He's not hiding it. Is the whole break with the CoF a super recent event that noone knows about? But how did it affect him then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T03:36:42-08:00","id":1525063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525046#post1525046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I read that I was so utterly confused. You have a hostile external element doing an abhorrent thing and you have reservations because... what? People don't know his allegiance? He's not hiding it. Is the whole break with the CoF a super recent event that noone knows about? But how did it affect him then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a guess, but given how de-centralised the Nation is and how the umbra is a risky place to visit, new might not just have reached the sept about the CoF break.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't justify not taking any action, especially as the Litany has a tenet for this that is still in W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T04:17:18-08:00","id":1525065,"title":"","content":"Bad worldbuilding (or more like the lack of it) in the W5 corebook is one of those problems that will haunt this game until somebody sits down and actually sets a solid foundation for the setting. Any statement about time raises questions in W5 because the W5 corebook is completely ambiguous on what happens when. And if in the course of writing future supplements you have writers at Renegade that only use the W5 corebook as a reference you will just get more examples of strange Garou behavior, I imagine. Litany, the Garou Nation, Septs, Auspices... those are all very untethered concepts with a lot of ambiguity if only the W5 corebook is used as a reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T08:35:35-08:00","id":1525071,"title":"","content":"Something the writer said in the Q&amp;A session stood out as being the opposite of what the W5 Core states. The W5 Core intimates that the Nation failed because it treated every problem as a nail and the Garou acted as hammers meaning that they used brute force and were quick to violence in situations where that only made things worse. Whereas the writer stated that the nation failed because they were too wishy-washy and could not come to any decisions about what should be done which is why things only got worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T08:43:34-08:00","id":1525072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525071#post1525071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something the writer said in the Q&amp;A session stood out as being the opposite of what the W5 Core states. The W5 Core intimates that the Nation failed because it treated every problem as a nail and the Garou acted as hammers meaning that they used brute force and were quick to violence in situations where that only made things worse. Whereas the writer stated that the nation failed because they were too wishy-washy and could not come to any decisions about what should be done which is why things only got worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I did not expect consistency, but this is pretty bad.<br /> <br /> Whether I like W5's setting or not, stuff like this needs to be consistent. Unless every game of W5 is set in its own universe, like with NWoD/CotfD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T09:33:29-08:00","id":1525073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525071#post1525071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something the writer said in the Q&amp;A session stood out as being the opposite of what the W5 Core states. The W5 Core intimates that the Nation failed because it treated every problem as a nail and the Garou acted as hammers meaning that they used brute force and were quick to violence in situations where that only made things worse. Whereas the writer stated that the nation failed because they were too wishy-washy and could not come to any decisions about what should be done which is why things only got worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The W5 core states that but what that writer is referring to is also there. From the introduction (pg 9): &quot;Almost all werewolves agree on what\u2019s going wrong, but they often disagree violently on how best to make the necessary changes (or even what those changes should be).\u200b&quot; I assume that's what the writer is referring to.<br /> <br /> But I always found that idea a bit confounding. If that's a problem inherent to Garou-society, you would never had something like the Garou-Nation to begin with. And explaining the change from when this wasn't a problem (so that the Garou-Nation could be formed) to the time when these differences turned into an issue (which is when the Garou-Nation fell) isn't covered by the W5 corebook, of course. Also, if you emphasize that idea as a fundamental problem of Garou-society, how come the idea of multi-Tribal Septs and Packs is still endorsed...? The logical follow-up would be more something like the faction-building the BNS-version engaged in. And why would the Fenrir disagreeing with the other Tribes be a big deal then if these disagreements are the norm...? &quot;Who knows&quot; can only do so much in covering up bad worldbuilding...<br /> <br /> The issue of how much of the W5 setting is ambiguous or just a blank slate will always come into conflict with all these supplements that aren't written with the idea that these ambiguities and blank spaces stay that way. The current WOD5E-approach may despise old lore/worldbuilding but it's not like they're writing these books with the idea that worldbuilding is completely left to the people at the table so that's what gets supported. Street-level-only, the Garou-Nation has fallen, the Cult of Fenris, it's the Age of Apocalypse... W5 still draws many lines in the sand where the setting gets confined and limiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T06:04:19-08:00","id":1525162,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Glyphs present in the pack, I can't help but see the history of W5 presented.<br /> <br /> We have a glyph for the Bite and Malady, both things in the BNS version.<br /> <br /> We have a glyph for Gaia's Howl, a remnant that was never elaborated on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T10:54:42-08:00","id":1525172,"title":"","content":"Homid and Glabro can't carve these glyphs due to not having claws, Lupus doesn't have claws long enough, and Hispo doesn't have the arm motion required. Curious, that.<br /> <br /> (Past editions required Crinos. But that couldn't be the case for W5 - all of the glyphs are super-elaborate and it would take multiple WP points just to carve one. Oops.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T12:56:35-08:00","id":1525176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525162#post1525162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the Glyphs present in the pack, I can't help but see the history of W5 presented.<br /> <br /> We have a glyph for the Bite and Malady, both things in the BNS version.<br /> <br /> We have a glyph for Gaia's Howl, a remnant that was never elaborated on.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> In some ways, it feels like what we got, in the end, was the lowest common denominator between the BNS version, the Hunters Entertainment version (headed by Karim Muammar) and the latest version (headed by Justin Achilli). And that's why the setting feels so lackluster...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525172#post1525172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homid and Glabro can't carve these glyphs due to not having claws, Lupus doesn't have claws long enough, and Hispo doesn't have the arm motion required. Curious, that.<br /> <br /> (Past editions required Crinos. But that couldn't be the case for W5 - all of the glyphs are super-elaborate and it would take multiple WP points just to carve one. Oops.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa... hey, c'mon! Didn't you read the W5 corebook? One Lupus scratched the entire Litany on a pile of stones. Those guys are hard workers! XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T23:08:54-08:00","id":1525193,"title":"","content":"Well its good they're developing the setting silly get writting aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T02:21:59-08:00","id":1525198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525193#post1525193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its good they're developing the setting silly get writting aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just that the way the W5 corebook did its worldbuilding is unsustainable. Like we've seen with Deepest of Wounds and it starts with &quot;Five years ago this happened...&quot;. At some point, you have to be at least somewhat solid on what the situation is. For example, I don't think the W5 corebook's take on the Garou-Nation (&quot;How long did it last? A century? A decade? Who knows. And it fell... but when? Who knows.&quot;) is sustainable either. Like, you have a Garou-elder NPC that says &quot;I remember the fall of the Garou-Nation.&quot; Bam! And now you have a timeline. Because the only way you could keep the approach of the corebook intact is if either no one ever talks about the Garou-Nation or when they talk about it, all they can say is that it once existed and now doesn't (which isn't really that much of a contribution in terms of worldbuilding). And if you keep to doing either of these things then really what was even the point of making it a part of the setting in the first place...? And so instead at some point, a Renegade-supplement will fill out this part to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T04:56:41-08:00","id":1525244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525198#post1525198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's just that the way the W5 corebook did its worldbuilding is unsustainable. Like we've seen with Deepest of Wounds and it starts with &quot;Five years ago this happened...&quot;. At some point, you have to be at least somewhat solid on what the situation is. For example, I don't think the W5 corebook's take on the Garou-Nation (&quot;How long did it last? A century? A decade? Who knows. And it fell... but when? Who knows.&quot;) is sustainable either. Like, you have a Garou-elder NPC that says &quot;I remember the fall of the Garou-Nation.&quot; Bam! And now you have a timeline. Because the only way you could keep the approach of the corebook intact is if either no one ever talks about the Garou-Nation or when they talk about it, all they can say is that it once existed and now doesn't (which isn't really that much of a contribution in terms of worldbuilding). And if you keep to doing either of these things then really what was even the point of making it a part of the setting in the first place...? And so instead at some point, a Renegade-supplement will fill out this part to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, it's a problem in v5 as well. The games cannot just spin their wheels forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T05:08:47-08:00","id":1525246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525244#post1525244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yeah, it's a problem in v5 as well. The games cannot just spin their wheels forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's the same for H5 as well. In the first supplement Lines Drawn By Blood you can end up working for a hunter-org in one of the chronicles while the corebook considered that an aboslute impossibility. But at its heart H5 is a game of mortal hunters vs the supernatural. Maintaining that hatred for hunter-orgs needlessly limits what you can do with the concept. And with W5 you can't maintain that &quot;Who knows&quot;-stance forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T00:36:27-08:00","id":1525294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525246#post1525246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, it's the same for H5 as well. In the first supplement Lines Drawn By Blood you can end up working for a hunter-org in one of the chronicles while the corebook considered that an aboslute impossibility. But at its heart H5 is a game of mortal hunters vs the supernatural. Maintaining that hatred for hunter-orgs needlessly limits what you can do with the concept. And with W5 you can't maintain that &quot;Who knows&quot;-stance forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the obvious things with h5 is just bringing in a book on imbued. Easy slam dunk since it throws hunter fans a bone and broadens the type of games available.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T02:38:10-08:00","id":1525302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525294#post1525294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the obvious things with h5 is just bringing in a book on imbued. Easy slam dunk since it throws hunter fans a bone and broadens the type of games available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, can you really trust the current Paradox/Renegade-writing-team to not still fuck it up somehow in the end... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ? I guess, we're gonna see how the upcoming V5 supplement Crimson Gutter will turn out that aims to make the Church of Caine a playable faction in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T03:12:28-08:00","id":1525303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525302#post1525302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, can you really trust the current Paradox/Renegade-writing-team to not still fuck it up somehow in the end... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ? I guess, we're gonna see how the upcoming V5 supplement Crimson Gutter will turn out that aims to make the Church of Caine a playable faction in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, that's just diet sabbat or langea sanctum in a setting we're it doesn't syngergise with 4 other political factions.<br /> <br /> Edit-i suppose that at least they're doing something with the setting but it's kinda silly that they won't just re implement Sabbat if they want a noddist sect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-10-2023, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T09:07:48-08:00","id":1525310,"title":"","content":"In all honesty? If you want to have a free'er setting than VtM, using the VtR covenants as an example is smart.<br /> <br /> But I think W5, unlike Hunter 5 and Vampire 5, suffers from how long it was in production and how much of its worldbuilding is focused on the word NO. Plus all the recent kerfluffle about it. I'm not sure what direction it CAN go, given the hard limits placed by the core/people in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T14:39:45-08:00","id":1525329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525294#post1525294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the obvious things with h5 is just bringing in a book on imbued. Easy slam dunk since it throws hunter fans a bone and broadens the type of games available.</div> </div> </div> </div>So obviously it's never going to happen, then. (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T05:02:48-08:00","id":1525370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525310#post1525310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty? If you want to have a free'er setting than VtM, using the VtR covenants as an example is smart.<br /> <br /> But I think W5, unlike Hunter 5 and Vampire 5, suffers from how long it was in production and how much of its worldbuilding is focused on the word NO. Plus all the recent kerfluffle about it. I'm not sure what direction it CAN go, given the hard limits placed by the core/people in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, one particular example of that is gonna be how Pack-Patron-Spirits are handled in the first W5 supplement Scent Of Decay. We already had those sisters whose Pack-Patron-Spirit was Athena and one of the adventures in that supplement is &quot;A Pound of Flesh: A rival pack and their patron spirit challenge Milton\u2019s Garou&quot;. Hopefully, that book comes with rules for freely choosing your group's Pack-Patron-Spirit. Because the W5 corebook doesn't let you do that. You <i>have to</i> pick a Tribe-Patron-Spirit as your Pack-Patron-Spirit. And it would suck to see yet another NPC-Garou-Pack that has this individualized choice for a Pack-Patron-Spirit while PC-Packs aren't allowed to do that (according to the rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T08:12:08-08:00","id":1525371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525302#post1525302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, can you really trust the current Paradox/Renegade-writing-team to not still fuck it up somehow in the end... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ? I guess, we're gonna see how the upcoming V5 supplement Crimson Gutter will turn out that aims to make the Church of Caine a playable faction in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Church of Caine is already a playable faction, though, they get quite the wordcount in both Camarilla and Cults of the Blood Gods: that they get upgraded to &quot;first tier&quot; status along the Camarilla and the Anarchs is the real &quot;&quot;&quot;metaplot&quot;&quot;&quot; advancement, we'll se if they stay true to their Cainite Heresy origins or make some other retcons.<br /> <br /> BTW, my players are more on the action side of things, so even when I use it I cannot take long time in delving in its philosophy, but I really love the whole Cainite Heresy thing, it's very distinct from both the Sabbat and the Lancea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-12-2023, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T13:23:54-08:00","id":1525386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1524705-new-w5-glyphs-released?p=1525371#post1525371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Church of Caine is already a playable faction, though, they get quite the wordcount in both Camarilla and Cults of the Blood Gods: that they get upgraded to &quot;first tier&quot; status along the Camarilla and the Anarchs is the real &quot;&quot;&quot;metaplot&quot;&quot;&quot; advancement, we'll se if they stay true to their Cainite Heresy origins or make some other retcons.<br /> <br /> BTW, my players are more on the action side of things, so even when I use it I cannot take long time in delving in its philosophy, but I really love the whole Cainite Heresy thing, it's very distinct from both the Sabbat and the Lancea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. For me, the question is: what do they actually mean with what's described in the blurb for the Crimson Gutter supplement then...? New Merits and Flaws, new Coterie-Types, new Loresheets... or is this book actually gonna retcon stuff from Camarilla and Cults of the Blood Gods... Well, the most disappointing would be to do neither, I think. For example, Blood Sigils talks about &quot;Vienna Zero&quot; but it never is developed enough to turn it into an actual story-hook.<br /> <br /> That's what was so great about the Onyx Path books for V5. You get enough worldbuilding to be usable as a jumping-off point. With Blood Sigils the cover-story for what happened in Vienna is mentioned - which is an an advancement in the metaplot so-to-speak. The Tremere HQ was taken out in this blatant way and now the world reacts. And what does Blood Sigils give you...? The Loresheet says that &quot;Hungarian fascists&quot; were blamed for the attack. It's absurd and it doesn't help that this is the <i>only </i>time it comes up in the book. This general dislike for lore/worldbuilding in WOD5E these days is really hampering the exploration of stuff like that.<br /> <br /> My biggest fear is that with the current direction of WOD5E, that section on the Church of Caine will just come off as bland because there's a fear to commit to any sort of lore/worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}